# AJX Tax — MVP overnight workflow

Before implementing any feature or screen, follow `docs/architecture/adr/024-overnight-workflow-mvp-foundation.md`, `docs/features/overnight-workflow-mvp.md`, and `docs/features/mvp-completion-gate.md`.

## Philosophy

**Simple. Reliable. Fast. Audit-ready.**

Prioritise polish, stability, and usability over additional features. First release must feel polished and complete even when advanced automation is deferred.

## MVP complete when the user can

1. Create or select a financial year.
2. Enter overnight counts manually by destination and month.
3. Upload supporting evidence.
4. Create destination sample days.
5. Enter receipts.
6. Complete sample days.
7. Calculate destination averages (traceable).
8. Produce a complete Tax Position (overnight claim + provenance).
9. Export an accountant summary.
10. Backup and restore data.

## Do not begin until MVP is complete

- AI / OCR classification
- Google Drive sync
- Roster interpretation / parsing

Stubs/adapters may exist with clear “coming later” messaging — never as dependencies.

## Non-negotiable product rules

- **Overnight table** = source of truth for overnight counts.
- **Roster** = evidence only.
- **Do not** redesign into a generic expense tracker.
- Tax Position displays the overnight-derived claim with full provenance (U11–U12).

## Also required

Product & engineering standards (`docs/standards/00-overview.md`, ADR-020) and commercial expansion (`docs/architecture/14-commercial-expansion.md`).
